                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="150X/151X" notBefore="1500" notAfter="1519" calendar="#gregorian">s. xvi in.</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_198">Eton, Buckinghamshire.
                        Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'Liber collegii [. . .] (first letter perhaps E) Donum Magistri
                        Guilielmi [. . .]ani quondam socii eiusdem collegii' (fol. 1r, at
                        top).</p><p>No doubt a gift to Eton from William Horman (d. 1532), fellow of
                        Eton from 1502 until his death. He was an author and bookman and the donor
                        of a considerable library to Eton. (See further Willoughby, Collegiate
                        Churches, 130–32.) The script, small, pointed, and very expert, is like
                        that of MS indexes, etc., in books belonging to Horman, e.g. Gloucester
                        Cathedral, MS 3.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Liber Thomæ Symes' (fol. 1r, at top): he
                     used the 'Liber' of the earlier inscription and wrote his name over 'Collegii
                     [. . .]'; he gave the copy to Winchester College, s. xvi/xvii.</provenance>
               </history>
